neral\/2024\/alaska\/trump-vs-harris\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/house\/general\/2024\/alaska\/at-large\/peltola-vs-begich-final-round\">AK-AL<\/a><strong><strong><br \/>2022:<\/strong><\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/senate\/general\/2022\/alaska\/murkowski-vs-tshibaka-final-round\">Senate<\/a> |\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/governor\/general\/2022\/alaska\/dunleavy-vs-gara-final-round\">Governor<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/house\/general\/2022\/alaska\/at-large\/palin-vs-peltola\">AK-AL<\/a><strong><strong><br \/>2020:<\/strong><\/strong>\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/president\/general\/2020\/alaska\/trump-vs-biden-vs-jorgensen\">President<\/a> |\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/senate\/general\/2020\/alaska\/sullivan-vs-gross\">Senate<\/a> |\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/house\/general\/2020\/alaska\/at-large\/young-vs-galvin\">AK-AL<\/a><strong><strong><br \/>2018:<\/strong><span>\u00a0<\/span><\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/governor\/general\/2018\/alaska\/dunleavy-vs-begich\">Governor<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2018\/house\/ak\/alaska_atlarge_district_young_vs_galvin-6699.html\">AK-AL<\/a><strong><br \/>2016:\u00a0<\/strong><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2016\/president\/ak\/alaska_trump_vs_clinton_vs_johnson_vs_stein-6114.html\">President<\/a>\u00a0|\u00a0<a href=\"https:\/\/www.realclearpolling.com\/polls\/epolls\/2016\/senate\/ak\/alaska_senate_murkowski_vs_metcalfe-5990.html\">Senate<\/a><strong><br \/>2014<\/strong>:\u00a0<a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/governor\/ak\/alaska_governor_parnell_vs_walker-5215.html\">Governor<\/a>\u00a0|<span>\u00a0<\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.realclearpolitics.com\/epolls\/2014\/house\/ak\/alaska_atlarge_district_young_vs_dunbar-5231.html\">AK-AL<\/a><strong><br \/><\/strong><\/p>"},"dataAnalysis":{"title":"Race Analysis","content":"<p>Alaska joined the Union as a political counterweight to Hawaii. Alaska was supposed to be the Democratic state, while Hawaii would be the Republican one. It worked out that way for a few years, but the party loyalties quickly switched\u2014Alaska became a staunchly Republican state by the 1970s, while Hawaii became equally Democratic.<\/p>\n<p>One of the earliest indicators that Alaska was headed toward the GOP was the party\u2019s first Senate win in a 1970 special election. Ted Stevens had been appointed to the Senate in 1968 to finish the term of Democratic Sen. Bob Bartlett, who had passed away, and won the election handily. He faced little trouble with re-election until 2008. That year, although he had been convicted on multiple felony counts (the verdict was later set aside) shortly before the election, Stevens lost by just over a percentage point to Democrat Mark Begich.<\/p>\n<p>Begich lasted a term before losing to former state Attorney General Dan Sullivan in 2014; Sullivan won handily against independent Al Gross in 2020. This cycle, however, seems to provide the toughest challenge of Sullivan\u2019s career. First, he\u2019s facing off against former Rep. Mary Peltola, the second Democrat to win a federal office in the state since the 1970s. Second, Alaska adopted a top-four primary and ranked-choice general-election system in the interim. Three Republicans are currently on the general-election ballot, along with Peltola. One of them (not coincidentally, Republicans claim) is also named Dan Sullivan.<\/p>\n<p>Democrats are counting on two things. First, they hope the Democratic trend in Alaska\u2019s presidential voting combines with a pro-Democratic environment and pushes Peltola ahead. Second, they hope that Republican voters cast their ballots for one of the two other Republican candidates and then either forget or decline to rank any other candidates, resulting in \u201cballot exhaustion.\u201d Alaska polling is notoriously inaccurate. We likely won't have a good indication of who will win this race until the morning after Election Day.<\/p>"},"showLineChart":1,"showBarChart":1,"showLineChartFirst":1,"sideCharts":{"charts_on_top":0,"left_chart_race_id":"7220","right_chart_race_id":"3658"},"show_final_results":0,"chart_data":{"chart_id":"7311","chart_axis_x":"1","chart_grid_x":"4","chart_axis_y":"1","chart_grid_y":"10","chart_min":"","chart_max":"","chart_start":"1776661200","chart_end":"","poll_id":"8754","chart_highlight":"#bbbb00","chart_days_extend":"7","chart_height":"360","chart_height_mobile":"360","chart_html5":"1","chart_main_percent":"70","chart_spread_percent":"30","chart_spread_range":"10","chart_name_in_tooltips":"1","chart_spread_force_0_y_axis":"1","chart_y_axis_min":"44","chart_y_axis_max":"52","chart_y_axis_min_m":"44","chart_y_axis_max_m":"52","chart_dates":{"7D":"0","14D":"0","30D":"0","MAX":"1"},"chart_dates_old":[{"period":"DD","count":"14","label":"7D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"21","label":"14D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"37","label":"30D","selected":"0"},{"period":"MAX","count":"1","label":"MAX","selected":"1"}],"chart_dates_mobile":{"7D":"0","14D":"0","30D":"0","MAX":"1"},"chart_dates_mobile_old":[{"period":"DD","count":"14","label":"7D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"21","label":"14D","selected":"0"},{"period":"DD","count":"37","label":"30D","selected":"0"},{"period":"MAX","count":"1","label":"MAX","selected":"1"}]}},"poll":[{"id":"8754","type":"rcp_average","pollster":"rcp_average","date":"9\/28 - 10\/16","confidenceInterval":"","sampleSize":"","marginError":"","partisan":"","candidate":[{"name":"Peltola","affiliation":"Democrat","value":"49.4","status":"1","id":"34872"},{"name":"Sullivan","affiliation":"Republican","value":"48.2","status":"1","id":"34871"}],"undecided":[],"sp